name issue_120_rtx_payload_padding
describe Wi-Fi to LTE handover with `cc v2`, `pacer v2` and `rtx v2`: padding is RTX payload padding first, as libwebrtc's RTPSender::GeneratePadding (#120)
# libwebrtc (CI compare-webrtc, issue_23_handover, 10 seeds): net.padding_kbps 0.6, net.rtx_kbps 460, freezes 4.3 (4528 ms).
# Before #120 the pacer queued 224 B placeholders that the sender filled with empty padding: 14.6 kbps of padding.
# Acceptance (issue #120): net.padding_kbps and net.rtx_kbps within the parity band of libwebrtc's. The freeze gap is not shown to
# come from padding and stays with #116.
cc v2
pacer v2
rtx v2
keyframe v2
duration 40s
at 0s  capacity=4000kbps delay=15ms jitter=5ms queue=200ms
at 15s down
at 16.5s up capacity=1200kbps delay=60ms jitter=15ms loss=1%
reverse at 0s delay=15ms
reverse at 15s down
reverse at 16.5s up delay=60ms
expect net.padding_kbps < 2
# Restored to >= 380 by #217 (was provisionally >= 330 after PR #186): the first transport feedback waits the
# generator's default 100 ms, as libwebrtc's Call does. Seed 1 393 kbps (main 344), 10 seeds 401 (main 394),
# libwebrtc 451.
expect net.rtx_kbps >= 380
expect net.rtx_kbps <= 600
